facts={
(24,5):('Stores session while retained restore initializer may recover intent; constructor does not load history or register pending. Summary says restore not exposed but actual later methods/XAML expose it, stale safety copy rather than absence.','RetainedRequest<RestoreBackupRequest> initializer','Restored intent global pending and visible recovery affordance.'),
(26,60):('Exposes history of backup/verify/restore records; list success is metadata only, not proof file exists now or restore tested.','LoadAsync','No backup or database files read by audit.'),
(40,16):('LastGoodBackup candidate requires Kind Backup, Status Succeeded and completion timestamp, but not Verified; detail labels verification separately. A latest unverified successful file displaces older verified backup headline.','LastGoodBackup Where','Operational wording should distinguish completed backup from proven recoverability.'),
(41,28):('Sorts successful backup candidates descending completion timestamp. No oldest/latest file filesystem check or age refresh timer.','LastGoodBackup OrderByDescending','Future timestamp clamp and clock skew tests.'),
(51,9):('Builds last backup time, whole MiB size and verification text from metadata. Uses machine local display, not Cairo explicitly; missing successful backup warns none. No restore or verify command invoked.','LastGoodBackup; ToLocalTime','Sub-MiB rounds0MB and future timestamp display.'),
(70,5):('Clamps negative elapsed minutes to zero then expresses minutes/hours/days, truncating fractional units. Cast large TotalMinutes to int can overflow extreme timestamps, normal file ages bounded.','DescribeAge -> Math.Max/int conversion','Clock skew/future and47/48hour boundaries.'),
(82,9):('Displays latest restore attempt by requested time, accepts Succeeded as success, Blocked separate and other statuses as failure. This recognizes actual backend success vocabulary unlike CompleteRestore UI014.','Backups.Where/OrderByDescending','Compare returned Succeeded after actual restore source only, never execute.'),
(84,41):('Filters metadata Kind exactly Restore; other casing/new record types omitted. No database state inferred from file name.','LastRestoreLine Where','Contract enum-string compatibility.'),
(84,85):('Chooses latest restore by RequestedAtUtc rather than completed time, so later blocked attempt can be headline over earlier success; copy says last attempt accordingly.','LastRestoreLine OrderByDescending','Concurrent attempts server guard and accurate record ordering.'),
(99,5):('Read load serialized by IsLoading only, not IsBusy/restore pending. Replaces records and notifies age/history fields; age does not tick after load, so stale threshold UI can lag until refresh.','Api.GetBackupsAsync; Backups.Clear/Add','Refresh during restore returns coherent snapshot? parent server challenge.'),
(114,62):('Orders backup history by request timestamp newest first. It does not filter failed/blocked records, preserving operational history.','LoadAsync OrderByDescending','History scale and unknown timestamps.'),
(128,5):('Requires idle and backup_manage then issues new backup command with server default directory, no retained key/helper in VM. IsBusy blocks root while in-flight, but unknown creation outcome not retained; existing pending restore is not checked, so direct action can create backup while restore unresolved.','Api.CreateBackupAsync; LoadAsync','Unknown restore with create enabled and unknown backup retry semantics independent challenge.'),
(151,5):('Requires idle and permission then requests verify selected record, distinguishes Verified versus other metadata. Says recoverable for verified file though VERIFYONLY does not prove full application recovery; no restore performed. Does not guard pending restore.','Api.VerifyBackupAsync; LoadAsync','Unknown restore competing verification and stale record ID server validation.'),
(186,5):('Busy callback notifies restore button/label and globally registers busy or retained restore. After failed/unknown restore busyfalse still blocks root but other Backup create/verify guards ignore retained pending.','AppSession.SetManagementOperationPending','Command affordance consistency during pending restore.'),
(194,5):('Target change only updates IsRestoreOpen. Durable restored intent can exist while target null and OpenRestore blocked, hiding retry overlay despite SubmitRestore supporting pending branch.','OnPropertyChanged(IsRestoreOpen)','XAML standalone retry panel absent in prior report; independent challenge.'),
(211,5):('Opens restore overlay only idle/no pending, resets reason/confirmation/PIN and captures metadata record. No permission check here; server may allow approved fallback via ResolveRestoreApproval. It does not itself restore.','RestoreTarget setter; RestoreNeedsApproval notification','Recovery target absent and malicious record kind server check.'),
(223,5):('Blocks close while busy or retained restore unknown. Normal close clears target but leaves reason/PIN text until next open. No journal deletion or database change.','RestoreTarget setter','Unknown outcome cannot dismiss; UI recovery reachability.'),
(230,5):('Replays retained restore request without current target; first send validates explicit reason/exact domain confirmation phrase, then approval and captured record/user. Busy covers await. No session/target generation beyond modal guards, no automatic execution on constructor.','ResolveRestoreApprovalAsync; CompleteRestoreAsync; RequiredRestorePhrase','Destructive command never runtime-tested; use synthetic DTO-only handler fixture.'),
(262,5):('Retained restore send accepts typed record, then compares success status to Completed while backend and own history display use Succeeded UI014. Confirmed successful restore thus shown incomplete; retained helper already cleared because HTTP success. Overlay remains, user may resubmit destructive action with fresh payload unless backend prevents.','_restore.SendAsync; LoadAsync; Status comparison','Independent backend handler challenge UI014; never execute restore to prove.'),
(264,56):('Forwards immutable retained restore DTO unchanged to actual server RestoreBackupAsync. This is destructive server boundary; reviewer invoked none and did not build a live request.','Api.RestoreBackupAsync','Transport mock only; actor/approval/confirmation and unknown retry semantics.'),
(285,5):('Requires dedicated approval only without own backup_manage, validates minimum PIN and issues backup_manage approval with reason. No LoginByPin or bearer mutation. Whether server requires approval in addition versus fallback must be read handler policy, not stale summary.','Api.IssueManagerApprovalAsync','Parent policy challenge; credential transport safety without actual PIN.')
}
